  wrongExp: "• <strong>Option A (Onycholysis):</strong> This is the distal separation of the nail plate from the nail bed. While present in psoriasis, it does not specifically refer to the yellowish-brown discoloration.<br>• <strong>Option C (Subungual hyperkeratosis):</strong> The accumulation of thick, scaly debris under the nail plate, common in both psoriasis and onychomycosis.<br>• <strong>Option D (Beau's lines):</strong> Transverse, band-like depressions in the nail plate caused by a temporary arrest of nail matrix growth due to severe systemic illness or trauma."
