  q: "A 65-year-old woman presents with a persistent, asymptomatic, reticulated (net-like) macular erythema and hyperpigmentation on the anterior aspect of both her thighs. She has a history of chronic lower back and hip pain and admits to resting a hot water bottle or electric heating pad on her thighs every evening for the past 6 months to stay warm. What is the diagnosis?",
